icked the trailer video  when i got the notification from warner  brothers  i'm not ashamed to admit that now in  another part of the first look  we can see the character ren sarazawa  standing in front of a control panel  with a distinct metallic titan shape on  it that has writings saying  system reading at maximum charge ren is  actually the son of hiroshira played by  ken watanabe in the prior movies  and it's clear that he's inherited his  father's understanding of the titans  and has managed to craft his own the  place that we see him in  is clearly a mechagodzilla control room  and this signifies to me that he is  definitely being used by the humans  now if you've been keeping up to date  with the plots and oppositions that have  been released for the movie  you'll know recently there was one drop  that said the terrorist group apex were  looking to find a way to wipe out all  the titans in one fell swoop  apex themselves are rumored to have  built the beast through wren  who has used the brain of the severed  godora head from king of the monsters  and the gigantic titan skeleton from the  2014 godzilla film  though he appears in a very small way in  the trailer  he's clearly going to be laced  throughout the film and this is even  shown in the logos which have a distinct  blue electricity  flowing through them now because of his  dad it's difficult to tell whether ren  is going to be a good or bad guy  but if toby maguire has told me one  thing it's that people with this haircut  tend to be completely evil however i do  think that he may have been tricked by  apex  who would have been like look i know i  knew your dad  in a way after i tried to kill but we  we'd love to have you on board  now though we know little about apex  apparently they are trying to lure kong  and godzilla out into the open  so that they can have the pair fight  against one another and then when the  winner is weakened  they'll simply send mechagodzilla in to  finish them off  not finish them off like that you dirty  bad boy now this technique is something  that we saw expect to demonstrate with  the siamese fighting fishing from russia  with love  and it's commonly a tactic used in most  vs movies  where the two opposing sides then team  up to take out the greater evil  so it definitely is a possibility that  mechagodzilla could be the one carrying  out the attacks on the cities  in order to make the real one look bad  i've even saw theories on my trailer  breakdown that said mecca could be  wearing a gigantic kevlar suit  that just makes him look like godzilla  and it's like when you were a kid and  used to stand on your mates shoulders  and wear a trench coat to sneak into the  cinema  also i've been told because i didn't  have any friends however i'm going to  say  something controversial something that  you might want to sit down for  if you hashtag team godzilla okay you  sitting down  all right well i don't actually think  that mechagodzilla is the one who's  doing most of the city smashing  and i think it is indeed godzilla which  pains me to say  now in one scene in the trailer we can  see him blasting out his atomic breath  and this then sweeps across and causes  many casualties in the explosion  that arise from it now it may be a  kevlar suit yeah  but i think that the trailer in several  ways is hinting to us that both the  titans are  under some form of control or another  with kong we see a young girl who holds  up an idol that seems to calm down the  gigantic ape  and throughout the teaser there's lip  service paid to the fact that the pair  have a special bond  whether he recognizes similarities in  her to the people that he's eaten in the  past we don't know  but we very much have this idea that it  can be manipulated in some form or  another  even if it's willingly similar to this i  believe that kong will be under the  control of apex  who rather than playing their hand have  found a way to manipulate godzilla  into going wild 